<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
	<key>CFBundleExecutable</key>
	<string>AgentMenu</string>
	<key>CFBundleIconFile</key>
	<string>AgentMenu</string>
	<key>CFBundleIdentifier</key>
	<string>dev.facens.agentmenu</string>
	<key>CFBundleName</key>
	<string>AgentMenu</string>
	<key>CFBundleDisplayName</key>
	<string>AgentMenu</string>
	<!-- The copyright line of the standard About panel, which the status
	     item's menu opens. Without this key the panel shows a version and
	     nothing else. Same statement as the SPDX header on every source
	     file. -->
	<key>NSHumanReadableCopyright</key>
	<string>Copyright © 2026 Andrea Giannangelo. GPL-3.0-or-later.</string>
	<key>CFBundlePackageType</key>
	<string>APPL</string>
	<key>CFBundleShortVersionString</key>
	<string>__VERSION__</string>
	<key>CFBundleVersion</key>
	<string>__BUILD__</string>
	<key>LSMinimumSystemVersion</key>
	<string>14.0</string>
	<key>LSUIElement</key>
	<true/>
	<key>NSHighResolutionCapable</key>
	<true/>
	<key>NSAppleEventsUsageDescription</key>
	<string>AgentMenu asks Finder for the front window's folder, and asks your terminal to open a tab and run the agent.</string>
	<!--
	Sparkle (U11 / R12, R14). The feed is served from the public
	repository's gh-pages branch, which is outside the blast radius of
	packaging/publish-public.sh — that script replaces the public working
	tree wholesale on every sync and would delete a feed kept on main
	(KTD6). The URL is frozen into every build that ships with it, which
	also freezes the public repository's name.
	-->
	<key>SUFeedURL</key>
	<string>https://facens.github.io/agentmenu/appcast.xml</string>
	<!--
	The public half of the project's EdDSA key, generated 2026-09-21 with
	Sparkle 2.10.0's generate_keys (U12). It is never regenerated: every
	shipped binary carries it, so a new key pair would orphan every
	installed copy. Its private half lives in 1Password and, for the
	promotion job, as the SPARKLE_EDDSA_PRIVATE_KEY secret of the
	release-promotion environment — see docs/releasing.md.

	The app still refuses to start the updater when this value is empty
	rather than checking a feed whose signatures it could not verify: a
	build produced before provisioning must not quietly update itself.
	-->
	<key>SUPublicEDKey</key>
	<string>JUHhLpaZMNYd+8iN2sfLV2Ll/0UpqQPoTlzQPSKVIqE=</string>
	<!--
	R14: present, and true, so no update-permission prompt appears on the
	second launch. Sparkle asks that question only when the key is absent;
	answering it here is what keeps a menu-bar app from opening a dialog
	the user never asked for. KTD9: both checking and installing are
	automatic by default, which is what the maintainer asked for, and the
	promotion gate is the human check that replaces the one this removes.
	-->
	<key>SUEnableAutomaticChecks</key>
	<true/>
	<key>SUAutomaticallyUpdate</key>
	<true/>
</dict>
</plist>
